The bug was caused by the exported dates being set to UTC instead of the local timezone, which led to incorrect date representations, particularly causing issues with daylight savings time adjustments. This misconfiguration was introduced in a previous commit that defaulted to UTC dates, not accounting for users in different time zones. The patch corrects this by explicitly setting the default timezone to the local time during the iCalendar export process.
